{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BNjCNNxncaTydCyPgMDndk","type":"tool_result","content":"17:# Letting Claude Code run `python3 ...` directly lets a mis-resolved PATH\n48:# entry, spawning a `python3 -c \"import sys...\"` subprocess every single\n61:  ver=$(python3 -c \"import sys; print(f\\\"{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}\\\")\" 2>/dev/null) || {\n62:    echo \"ERROR: python3 not found or invocable. Framework requires Python >=3.9.\" >&2\n63:    exit 3\n71:    exit 3\n80:# was forking an extra `python3 -c` subprocess per invocation. Removed\n83:# JSON-parse call INSIDE the existing per-invocation python3 spawn\n127:# `python3` exists, 5 `command -v` failures + 1 spawn of `python -c\n201:  # Emit \"MAJOR MINOR\" from `python --version` output (e.g. \"Python 3.12.3\")\n243:  # in the cache-miss branch. The gate's `python3 -c ...` spawn is ~15-20ms\n293:  exit 0\n301:  exit 0\n310:  exit 0\n314:# PLAN-156 Wave 2 (SENT-GK-A) — decision→exit chokepoint.\n319:# deny on **exit 2** in addition to the stdout JSON (probes:\n321:# block, deny-emit and process-exit were DECOUPLED: `write_decision` only\n322:# wrote stdout and the shim `exec`'d the hook, so the hook's own exit 0\n323:# became the process exit — a correct deny could still fail OPEN on a\n328:# ## The rule: decision-derived, never exit-code-derived\n330:#   emitted deny          -> exit 2   (a decision was made: enforce it)\n331:#   emitted allow / {}    -> exit 0\n337:# Reading the DECISION rather than the hook's exit code is what keeps\n340:# gate pattern) exits 2, while a bare interpreter crash with no decision\n347:# lacuna (h) confirms exit 2 is INERT on Codex; if not, the mapping is\n348:# adapter-aware.\" Lacuna (h) found exit 2 is NOT inert on Codex — it is an\n353:# its own (grok P2, codex JSON-deny, claude JSON-block); the exit code is\n355:# an observable exit code with no enforcement gain, while breaking every\n356:# existing test that pins \"deny -> exit 0\" — a large blast radius for zero\n358:# that tightens the docs.x.ai \"deny REQUIRES exit 2\" rule is covered) where\n362:# unconditional EXIT map anyway: on grok a `block` with exit 2 STILL\n363:# fail-opens (P5 — malformed output beats the exit code). It is solved by\n366:# routes through this shim (hooks/tests/test_exit2_chokepoint.py). A named\n373:# fail-OPENs on `{\"decision\":\"block\"}` EVEN WITH exit 2 (probe P5). This\n374:# exit map is the secondary half; the meta-test asserts BOTH.\n377:# release turns exit-2-hostile; the arming check surfaces the override).\n382:#   - exit-2 mapping (deny->exit 2): belt-and-suspenders. CEO_HOOK_EXIT_MAP=0\n383:#     turns this off (a future grok release that makes exit-2 hostile).\n401:  # block on grok, so neither the rewrite nor the exit map should touch it.\n409:# Registered hooks have invocation deadlines: exit must leave spool work pending.\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 40]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e57f479-9c5a-4eb5-b16f-bf776385516b","uuid":"20259553-21c3-4104-a2cb-1c931f3ee7dd","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:27:47.742Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"17:# Letting Claude Code run `python3 ...` directly lets a mis-resolved PATH\n48:# entry, spawning a `python3 -c \"import sys...\"` subprocess every single\n61:  ver=$(python3 -c \"import sys; print(f\\\"{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}\\\")\" 2>/dev/null) || {\n62:    echo \"ERROR: python3 not found or invocable. Framework requires Python >=3.9.\" >&2\n63:    exit 3\n71:    exit 3\n80:# was forking an extra `python3 -c` subprocess per invocation. Removed\n83:# JSON-parse call INSIDE the existing per-invocation python3 spawn\n127:# `python3` exists, 5 `command -v` failures + 1 spawn of `python -c\n201:  # Emit \"MAJOR MINOR\" from `python --version` output (e.g. \"Python 3.12.3\")\n243:  # in the cache-miss branch. The gate's `python3 -c ...` spawn is ~15-20ms\